UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Declarer always takes 4 spades, 3 hearts, 1 diamond, and 2 clubs for 10 tricks. The two chances to try for an overtrick are either KQ of diamonds in the North hand or more likely a 3-3 clubs.|
PG| ***** 19 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So to try for an overtrick declarer should probably duck a club right away and can then play @CA and @CK to find out if clubs break or not.|
PG| ***** 20 ***** |


